    hookIntro:
      "'New drop, don't miss out!' performs about as well as a banner ad, which is to say barely at all, and it's still the default hook for most product launch posts because it's the fastest thing to type at 11pm the night before a launch goes live. Ecommerce founders have real stories behind their products — a manufacturing problem solved after three failed sample runs, a customer complaint that became the whole reason for a redesign, a sourcing decision that took four months longer than planned but meant the product could actually be made ethically — and lead with generic urgency instead, because urgency feels like the marketing move even when it isn't the interesting part of the story. The scarcity language doesn't fail because it's dishonest, it fails because it's identical to every other launch post a shopper scrolled past that morning, and nobody stops for the fortieth 'don't miss out' of the week. CarouseLabs finds the actual story behind the product and puts it first, saving the urgency and the call-to-action for further down the post, where it belongs once someone's actually reading. The story was usually sitting in a support ticket or a team Slack thread the whole time — the work isn't inventing something new, it's noticing what's already there and giving it the opening line instead of burying it under the same scarcity language every other brand in the category is running that same week.",
