    metaTitle: "Most Consultants Only Post the Results Slide. Here's the Rest of the Story, Mapped to a Week.",
    metaDescription:
      "Pick an engagement to walk through. Get a topic for each stage — diagnosis, strategy, implementation, results — in 5 minutes.",
    hookIntro:
      "A consulting engagement moves through the same rough stages every time — diagnosis, strategy, implementation, results — and most consultants only ever post about the results slide, skipping the parts of the process that actually demonstrate how you think. The diagnosis stage, where you actually found the root problem underneath a client's symptom, is the single most impressive part of the work and the part almost nobody ever writes about, even though it's the stage that most directly demonstrates the judgment a client is actually paying for. The strategy stage, where you reframed the whole approach, gets summarized in one throwaway line inside a longer case study instead of standing as its own post, even though the reframe itself is usually the single hardest and most valuable thing a consultant contributes. And the implementation stage — the messy, week-to-week reality of what actually changed — gets skipped entirely in favor of jumping straight from \"here's the plan\" to \"here's the outcome,\" as if the hardest part of consulting simply didn't happen. That gap costs more than it seems: a results-only post lets a skeptical prospect assume the number came easily, or worse, wonder if it's exaggerated, while a full arc gives them a process they can actually evaluate and trust. CarouseLabs builds a week that walks through the full arc of how an engagement actually works, not just the highlight at the end, so a prospective client sees the thinking that produced the result, not just the number that makes for a good screenshot.",
