    hookIntro:
      "Your course probably has eight or ten modules and you only ever preview the same one or two in your content, over and over, because picking a different one each time takes more thought than it seems like it should. The opening module, the one with the flashiest hook, gets referenced constantly, propped up as the course's entire personality even though it's often the least representative module of the actual curriculum's depth. Module six, the one that actually solves the problem most students say was the real turning point in their reviews, has maybe never been mentioned publicly at all, sitting completely unmarketed despite being the module students bring up unprompted the most. Course creators sit on a whole curriculum's worth of preview material and use a tiny fraction of it, which means a prospective buyer only ever sees a sliver of what they'd actually be paying for, and an existing student who already bought never gets reminded that a module they haven't finished yet might be exactly the one they need. The two over-used modules end up doing all the marketing work for the entire course, while modules that took just as long to build and often deliver more value sit completely invisible in the sales pitch, undersold not because they're weaker but simply because nobody got around to previewing them. CarouseLabs rotates through your actual modules to build a week that doesn't repeat itself, so the curriculum's full depth becomes visible over time instead of staying flattened into the same two modules everyone's already seen previewed a dozen times.",
